meta {
  name: List Objects
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/schema/{{connectionId}}/objects
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~schema: public
  ~kind: procedure
}

docs {
  The objects a database keeps beside its data, read live: procedures, functions, views and triggers in a schema (Postgres/MSSQL); views, indexes and validation rules (MongoDB); index templates, ingest pipelines, aliases and ILM policies (Elasticsearch — Elastic-managed ones are skipped).

  Each entry is { schema, name, kind, args?, parent? }: `args` (Postgres routines) are the identity argument types that tell overloads apart; `parent` is a trigger's table. `kind` filters to one kind; `parent` is also a MongoDB index's collection.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) plus **read** capability for the connection's environment — 403 otherwise (admins hold every environment).

  Errors: 503 { error, code: "CONNECTION_FAILED" } when the database host is
  unreachable (network); 500 { error } for other introspection failures.
}
